<div id="formulaPop" class="popup"><button onclick="closePop('formulaPop')">Close</button><h3>Formula Sheet - SMS 3380</h3><p><b>DB Pension:</b> Pension = Accrual x Final Salary x Years | <b>Commutation:</b> Lump Sum = Pension Given Up x Commutation Factor | <b>DC Fund:</b> Fund = Contributions Accumulated with Interest | <b>Funding Level:</b> Assets / Liabilities x 100% | <b>Contribution:</b> Total = Employer + Employee | <b>Transfer Value:</b> PV of Benefits Preserved | <b>Annuity:</b> Pension = Fund / Annuity Factor</p></div>
<div id="glossPop" class="popup"><button onclick="closePop('glossPop')">Close</button><h3>Glossary - SMS 3380</h3><p><b>Pension:</b> income in retirement. <b>DB:</b> defined benefit - pension promised by formula. <b>DC:</b> defined contribution - pension depends on fund. <b>NSSF:</b> National Social Security Fund, Kenya. <b>Occupational scheme:</b> employer pension scheme. <b>Accrual:</b> rate pension builds up, e.g. 1/60. <b>Commutation:</b> giving up part of pension for lump sum. <b>Vesting:</b> when benefits become yours. <b>Funding:</b> having enough assets to pay promises. <b>RBA:</b> Retirement Benefits Authority, Kenya regulator. <b>Annuity:</b> regular income for life.</p></div>
<div class="topic active" id="topic1">
<h2>Topic 1: Introduction to Pensions and Retirement</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~30 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Define pension, explain why pensions are needed, explain retirement ages.</p>
<p>A pension is income in retirement - when you stop working, you still need money for food, rent, medicine.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Why pensions are needed:</b> 1. People live longer after retirement. 2. No salary after retirement. 3. Family cannot always support. 4. Inflation eats savings.</p><p><b>Retirement ages in Kenya:</b> Normal retirement 60, early retirement 50, late retirement up to 70, ill-health retirement any age if medically unfit.</p><p><b>Three pillars:</b> 1. State - NSSF. 2. Occupational - employer scheme. 3. Personal - individual pension, savings.</p></div>
