<h2>Topic 3: Retirement Benefits - Pension, Lump Sum, Commutation</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~40 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain retirement pension, explain lump sum, calculate commutation.</p>
<p>On retirement you may take part as lump sum (cash) and the rest as monthly pension. Giving up pension for cash is commutation.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Example:</b> Pension 600000 per year. You commute 1/3. Pension given up = 200000. Commutation factor = 12. Lump sum = 200000 x 12 = 2400000. Remaining pension = 400000 per year.</p><p><b>Why commute?</b> To pay off loan, build house, start business, pay school fees. Why not commute all? You need monthly income for life.</p><p><b>Annuity:</b> If you have DC fund 12000000 and annuity factor 12, pension = 12000000 / 12 = 1000000 per year.</p></div>
