<h2>Topic 4: Death and Withdrawal Benefits</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain death in service, death after retirement, withdrawal, transfer values.</p>
<p>Not everyone reaches retirement. Schemes must pay if a member dies or leaves early.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Death in service:</b> Lump sum to dependants, e.g. 3 x salary, plus spouse pension, plus return of contributions.</p><p><b>Death after retirement:</b> Spouse pension, e.g. 50% of member pension, plus guarantee period - if member dies within 5 years, balance paid.</p><p><b>Withdrawal:</b> Member leaves before retirement. Gets own contributions + interest, plus part of employer contributions if vested. Or transfer value - PV of preserved benefits moved to new scheme.</p><p><b>Vesting:</b> When employer benefits become yours. In Kenya, often after 1-3 years.</p></div>
