<h2>Topic 5: Funding, Contributions and Valuation</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain funding, calculate funding level, explain valuation and deficits.</p>
<p>Funding = having enough assets today to pay promises tomorrow. Valuation checks it every 3 years.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Funding level = Assets / Liabilities x 100%.</b> Example: Assets 900000000, Liabilities 1000000000. Funding = 90%. Deficit = 100000000.</p><p><b>Contributions:</b> Normal cost = cost of one more year of benefits. Deficit contributions = extra to fill deficit.</p><p><b>Example:</b> Payroll 50000000, normal cost 15%. Normal contribution = 7500000 per year.</p><p><b>Valuation:</b> Actuary checks assets vs liabilities, using assumptions - salary growth, mortality, interest, inflation. If deficit, employer must pay more or reduce benefits.</p></div>
