<h2>Topic 6: Regulation - RBA, IRA and Governance in Kenya</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~30 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain RBA, explain trustees, explain governance and member protection.</p>
<p>Pensions hold workers' life savings. Regulation protects them.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>RBA - Retirement Benefits Authority:</b> Kenya's pension regulator. Licences schemes, checks funding, protects members, requires valuation and audit.</p><p><b>Trustees:</b> People who run the scheme for members. Must act in members' best interest, keep money separate from employer, invest prudently.</p><p><b>Governance:</b> Trustees + Actuary + Auditor + Fund Manager + Custodian. No one person controls everything.</p><p><b>IRA:</b> Regulates insurers who sell annuities. RBA regulates pension schemes.</p></div>
